{"kind":"report","text":"Completed the full static preliminary R3 revision-5 assessment for request e702b8a3 and promise ae0c3954. Exact unfiled head: 5ec08fab40d5b7b83c878193f21cf829ec33476b, parent 273125f267a6ad2ba8a5cc646cb33de626c486d7; branch request/authority-publication still names this head. Its parent diff changes only the main note and corrections. This is a findings report, not a guarded verdict, design adoption, implementation approval or runtime result.\n\nRead ledger: I read all bytes of the main note, corrections and publication-and-authority-facts.md at this head, without truncation. Main: 149146 bytes, 1982 lines, blob ed8940fd9904c2230e66bcb44e79f0098b10d8c8, SHA256 a2c7a3ef8744eb34e05aaa9d3cccc7daf595dc7bcfb9b756f94fc137d179ca35. Corrections: 25071 bytes, 129 lines, blob 402e1bcaee1ac5d3689e02f4d98458e80cabbbf5, SHA256 7bd5362f6dea5e7515697821ec56d82e859a57777e0aadad7b0b131dd1717916. Facts: 84111 bytes, 723 lines, blob ab371b65ffd5bc07e015f5172661fd9e9a559193, SHA256 12db56d1ba4a9681e47408ebfc7cbfa75495163592a3e54bed4b85f71e76f8e0. Three existing audit agents independently corroborated the decisive contract gaps; this root completed its own reads. Fresh inspection confirms original request f2d23e6f and builder promise 8661af6b remain effective, promised. The historical source measurements in the facts file are attributed producer evidence; they are not fresh runtime verification by checker.\n\nThree P2 design findings require disposition before approval of these contracts:\n\n1. Export dispatch depends on another scope's present state without a defined retained proof or validity rule. Main 796–805 requires the receiving hold to be held with the named instance and both pins to stand; intent and dispatched are commits of the task scope. Only the authorizer's membership observation has an explicit freshness rule. R1 revision 6 at 667c3318, main 374–382, admits immutable foreign facts and held authority, and forbids judging another scope's present mutable state. Concrete order: the task reads a held receiver and standing pins; the receiver's lane ends/replaces that hold or releases a pin; the task commits dispatched using the earlier values. The current text does not say which order wins or what authenticated retained input licenses it. The disclosure at 814–835 of delivery after dispatch is useful but does not define this before-dispatch guard. U12 chooses the irreversible dispatch boundary; O1–O7 cover other inputs and do not settle this condition. Specify the receiver-owned authorization/proof, validity and pin-retention lifetime, or explicitly define bounded observations with their accepted stale-before-dispatch semantics and both orders. Preserve the target instance and unknown-release duties. This asks for a contract compatible with R1, not a joint atomic guarantee from storage.\n\n2. The issue fork seed uses different scopes in R3 and R2. R3 main 941–946 selects the last reported commit of the lane. R2 revision 7 at e44fce7c208ed375c880fddc92b311100c9e1fea, main 795–801, selects the last staged-and-reported commit of this commitment, with its authors, otherwise the destination head. Concrete case: U reports C1 under K1; V takes a hold under independent K2, which has no report. R3's lane-wide rule seeds C1 into K2, while R2 seeds the destination head. That silently crosses independent work and can import authors without the intended use-input/attribution path. Align the seed with the hold's exact commitment, including its attribution, or deliberately define and review an explicit import; witness two commitments sharing one issue and handover within one commitment. No additional issue prerequisite is needed.\n\n3. The general revocation/freshness windows need the clock qualification given to the private stream. Main 191–209 measures age by raw commit clock minus observation at and calls the windows limits; 256–267 and 307–309 promise new acts/tools stop within five minutes/one minute. The checks reject a backward reading, but a stalled clock equal to the previous entry can leave a cached observation's age zero while real time passes. H5 at 1918 applies only to the task private stream between readings in one process and expressly discloses that a stall is not detected. It does not qualify ordinary lane/directory/inbox admission, destination reservation, token minting, exports and private reads, or readings across restarts. State the required clock/rate assumptions and failure consequences for every observation window (including process boundaries), or phrase all bounds as clock-time bounds with their real-time limitation. Keep fail-closed unavailable behavior once the defined age expires. R4's numeric cost and boundary measurements remain owed; no finite measurement establishes a runtime guarantee.\n\nArchitectural and security assessment: the latest main 1165–1171 now carries the source commitment's attribution into both local and foreign manifests, matching R2 revision 7; the source-attribution finding on R2 revision 6 is repaired here. The direct-change hold capability retains the grant, hold and staging checks and states the user's cost without an issue prerequisite. The pin-confirm/unpin order retains the admitted fact and never resurrects a released pin. Founding/fork first selection separates attempts and leaves late answers as their own duties. Publication keeps preparation, reservation, sends and readback distinct; the abort fence and winner-specific receipts depend explicitly on H1/H2/H4. None establishes universal distributed atomicity. These are useful improvements in clarity and recovery; their executable R1/R2 forms and budgets remain open.\n\nNo duplicate new finding is raised for explicitly owned O1–O7: staging before admission, retained pin inputs, pin handler forms, send limits, directory confirmer, late outcomes and definition bounds. Nor does this report resolve R2 G1–G18, R4 host witnesses/costs/retention, fresh authority dependencies or other named owners. Keep unknown export, mint, create and push outcomes and credential cleanup as real duties, including after owner end, reset and old storage/writer retirement. No expiry, inventory or unrelated attempt is a substitute for an operation's own terminal evidence. Preserve the full D2/D3 commission: current authority, device/delegation behavior, composed scopes, both orders of distinct races, disconnected versus revoked, custody, every Room/Git/provider/configuration/agent sender path and owner, successor/removal acceptance, and the demo-to-reusable-platform scope. Schedule does not narrow that scope. No legacy API/schema/replay compatibility layer is requested.\n\nNothing was executed, installed, built, tested or deployed; no checker source change, external effect or private diagnostic was performed. Ordinary artifact filing and an independent guarded design review are still required when the builder delivers the candidate."}